# The ritual chamber (death_house_dungeon_2). The cult's shades stand beside the altar and demand a death.
# Started by talking to the shades (NPC cult_shades) or examining the altar before the choice is made.
# REFUSE: Lorghoth wakes; the party runs (a Dexterity check, or a fight with the shades) or stands and fights
#         (lorghoth_rises: deliberately far beyond the level 2 budget). The house then turns on them (escape.dialogue).
# SACRIFICE: the player chooses a party member, who dies; the house is satisfied and lets the rest walk out.
# Lore (death_house_lore >= 4) or a denunciation (Religion) gives a head start against Lorghoth.

~ altar_prop
if flag.death_house_refused or flag.death_house_sacrificed
  narrate examine:altar
  -> END
endif
-> start

~ start
Narrator: Robed figures made of shadow stand around the stone altar, faces hidden, voices joined. The chant has been rising since the stairs. Here, you can finally make out the words.
cult_shades: One must die. One must die. One must die.
interject name:silvain_aster: Technically, everyone must. I suspect they mean sooner.
if not name:silvain_aster
  interject class:wizard: Everyone dies eventually. I assume they're in a hurry.
endif
if flag.death_house_promised_walter
  cult_shades: You came for the child. The child was ours first. One must die.
endif
quest death_house the_altar
-> choose

~ choose
* Who are you? -> who
* What is that heap in the corner? -> heap
* [if not flag.death_house_altar_denounced] [Religion DC 14] Denounce their creed in the name of the dawn. -> denounce_ok | denounce_fail
* [if flag.death_house_lore >= 4 and not flag.death_house_head_start] We know what you are, and what sleeps in that heap. -> know
* [Wizard] Offer them a familiar instead: a spirit, not a life. -> familiar
* Refuse. Nobody here is dying for you. -> refuse
* Give them what they ask: one of you, on the altar. -> sacrifice
* Back away from the altar. -> back_away

~ back_away
cult_shades: One must die. We will wait. We are very good at waiting.
-> END

~ who
cult_shades: We fed the house. The house fed the one below. The one below waits for the lord to remember us. One must die.
-> choose

~ heap
Narrator: A mound of rot and old rushes, taller than a man, steaming faintly in the cold. It rises and falls, very slowly, like something asleep.
if flag.death_house_dollhouse_altar_seen
  Narrator: The lump of grey clay beside the dollhouse altar. It was never clay.
endif
interject name:tamsin_tealeaf: It's breathing. Why is it breathing. Heaps don't breathe.
-> choose

~ denounce_ok
set death_house_altar_denounced
set death_house_head_start
Narrator: {name}'s voice rings off the stone, and the shades flinch back from it like smoke from an opened door. The chant stumbles. The heap stirs, but slowly. Slowly.
interject name:hedda_ironvow: Mm. They remember what dawn is. Good.
-> choose

~ denounce_fail
set death_house_altar_denounced
Narrator: The words come out strong, and the chant swallows them whole without slowing.
-> choose

~ know
set death_house_head_start
Narrator: You say it plainly: the cult and the Dursts, the children left in the attic, the baby given on this altar, the thing in the heap, the lord who never wanted any of it.
Narrator: For the first time in years the chant falters. Knowing a story is a kind of power over it.
interject name:silvain_aster: Footnoted and cross-referenced. They hate that.
-> choose

~ familiar
cult_shades: A spirit does not die. It only goes home. One must die.
interject name:silvain_aster: I wasn't really offering. I was establishing the rules. Rules established.
-> choose

~ refuse
Narrator: The chanting stops. In the silence, the heap of refuse takes a long, wet breath.
cult_shades: Then the house will have all of you.
set death_house_refused
interject name:ilse_varga: Fall back to the stairs. Don't run until I say. ...Run.
if not name:ilse_varga
  interject class:fighter: Back to the stairs. Keep together. Go!
endif
if flag.death_house_head_start
  Narrator: Because you knew to watch the heap, you are already moving when it begins to stand.
endif
-> refuse_choice

~ refuse_choice
* Run for the stairs. -> run
* Stand and fight it here. -> stand

~ run
if flag.death_house_head_start
  Narrator: You are through the antechamber before the thing in the heap has finished standing up. Behind you it says its own name in a voice like a drain. Lorghoth. Lorghoth.
  -> fled
endif
check Dexterity DC 12 -> run_clear | run_caught

~ run_clear
Narrator: You make the archway as the heap rises behind you, wet and enormous, its tendrils closing on the place where you stood a moment ago.
-> fled

~ run_caught
Narrator: The shades boil up out of the floor between you and the stairs, hooded and hungry. They mean to hold you here until the heap can stand.
combat shades_harry

~ fled
Narrator: Lorghoth the Decayer is too vast for the narrow ways and too slow for the stairs. The house is neither.
-> END

~ stand
if flag.death_house_head_start
  Narrator: You have a moment to choose your ground before it reaches you. Use it.
  combat lorghoth_rises_late
endif
Narrator: It stands, and keeps standing, until its top brushes the ceiling.
combat lorghoth_rises

~ sacrifice
Narrator: The chant softens, almost kindly. The altar is waiting for one of you to lie down on it. Whoever does will not get up.
interject name:hedda_ironvow: No. Listen to me. This is the one thing we do not do. Not for a door. Not for anything.
if not name:hedda_ironvow
  interject class:cleric: Don't. Whatever this buys us, we'll be paying for it forever.
endif
interject name:ilse_varga: I've lost a company. I'm not giving one of you to a hole in the floor.
* Choose who lies on the altar. They die, and the house lets the rest of you go. -> sacrifice_done
* No. Not this. -> choose

~ sacrifice_done
# The player picks a living party member, who dies for good (the `sacrifice` statement).
sacrifice
set death_house_sacrificed
Narrator: It is quick, and it is quiet, and afterward none of you can remember who held the knife.
cult_shades: One has died. The house is satisfied.
Narrator: The shades unravel into the dark. The heap sighs and settles deeper into its sleep. Far above you, every lock in the house turns over, one after another, like a man cracking his knuckles.
if flag.death_house_children_riding
  Narrator: Two small cold weights slip out of two of you and away up the stairs, back to the attic where the house keeps its children.
  set death_house_children_riding = false
endif
set death_house_completed
quest death_house escaped_sacrificed
xp milestone
Narrator: The way out is open. Nothing in this house will stop you leaving now. Nothing in it needs to.
-> END
